{"id": "2026-08-14-news-swiss-gdp-rebounds-on-pharma-exports", "date": "2026-08-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss GDP rebounds on pharma exports", "summary": "Swiss GDP grew 1.5% in a first SECO estimate for Q2 2026, driven by a 15.2% rebound in chemical and pharmaceutical exports.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/economie/le-pib-de-la-suisse-progresse-de-1-5-au-2e-trimestre-porte-par-la-chimie-et-la-pharmacie", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Swiss GDP rebounded sharply in the second quarter of 2026, growing 1.5% in a first estimate from the State Secretariat for Economic Affairs (SECO), after 0.4% in Q1. SECO attributed the jump to a strong recovery in the chemical and pharmaceutical industry — the country's largest export sector — whose exports rose 15.2% quarter-on-quarter after four straight quarters of decline; broader industrial exports grew 1.7%. SECO issued only a brief flash release and will publish detailed figures on 3 September.", "why": "the headline looks strong, but much of it is one narrow, volatile sector: a large part of the pharma bounce reflects shipments front-loaded ahead of US tariffs (Washington set an import levy of 12.5% on Swiss goods at the end of July), so the reader should treat 1.5% as a preliminary, lopsided figure rather than proof of broad-based strength — the industry lobby Swissmem has warned that recent industrial growth rests \"on a small number of companies.\"", "thread_id": "2026-08-14-news-swiss-gdp-rebounds-on-pharma-exports", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-14", "event_date": "2026-08-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland", "SECO", "Swissmem"]}
{"id": "2026-08-14-news-fatal-crash-shuts-seelisberg-tunnel", "date": "2026-08-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Fatal crash shuts Seelisberg tunnel", "summary": "A fatal collision closed the A2 Seelisberg tunnel on the north-south axis for several hours on 14 August.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/wichtige-verkehrsverbindung-toedlicher-unfall-im-seelisberg-tunnel-seit-stunden-gesperrt", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A fatal crash closed the A2 Seelisberg tunnel on the morning of Friday 14 August, cutting the main north–south road axis for several hours. The tunnel, a critical link on the route toward the Gotthard, was shut in both directions while emergency services worked at the scene; police confirmed at least one death. The closure forced traffic onto slower valley roads during the summer holiday travel season.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-08-14-news-fatal-crash-shuts-seelisberg-tunnel", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-14", "event_date": "2026-08-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Seelisberg Tunnel", "A2", "Switzerland"]}
{"id": "2026-08-14-news-white-house-accuses-40-nations-over-china-tariff", "date": "2026-08-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "White House accuses 40 nations over China tariffs", "summary": "A White House trade-office report accuses more than 40 countries of helping China evade US tariffs via transshipment, at an estimated 19-26 billion dollars a year.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/8/14/us-accuses-dozens-of-countries-of-helping-china-avoid-trumps-tariffs", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["economy", "geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The White House accused more than 40 countries of helping China dodge US tariffs, in a report its trade office published on Thursday 13 August. The Office of Trade and Manufacturing Policy — headed by trade adviser Peter Navarro — said Chinese goods are routed through third countries and relabelled to disguise their origin, a practice it branded the \"Great Transshipment Scam\" and estimated costs the US Treasury 19–26 billion dollars a year in lost tariff revenue. It named the EU, Mexico, Canada, India, Japan and South Korea as the biggest \"enablers,\" alongside Indonesia, Thailand, Malaysia and Cambodia.", "why": "the \"scam\" framing and the dollar figures are the administration's own, and the legal footing is contested — the US Supreme Court struck down Trump's sweeping \"Liberation Day\" tariffs in February, and 25 Democratic-led states are challenging the replacement levies in court as a pretext to reimpose them; none of the named governments had responded, so read the report as a negotiating move to pressure trading partners, not a settled finding.", "thread_id": "2026-08-14-news-white-house-accuses-40-nations-over-china-tariff", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-14", "event_date": "2026-08-13", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["United States", "China", "Peter Navarro", "European Union"]}
{"id": "2026-08-14-news-ukraine-civilian-toll-hits-highest-since-2022", "date": "2026-08-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Ukraine civilian toll hits highest since 2022", "summary": "UN monitors recorded 437 civilians killed and 2,610 injured in Ukraine in July, the highest monthly toll since May 2022.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-monthly-civilian-casualties-highest-since-2022/live-78351269", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics", "world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Civilian casualties in Ukraine hit their highest monthly level since May 2022, according to the UN human rights monitoring mission's July figures. The mission (OHCHR) recorded 437 civilians killed and 2,610 injured in July — a roughly 30% rise on June and about 70% higher than July 2025 — driven largely by long-range missile and drone barrages on cities, including a 2 July assault on Kyiv using dozens of missiles and hundreds of drones.", "why": "the numbers quantify what the shift to mass drone-and-missile strikes on urban areas is doing to civilians, and mark the deadliest stretch for non-combatants since the early weeks of Russia's 2022 full-scale invasion.", "thread_id": "2026-08-14-news-ukraine-civilian-toll-hits-highest-since-2022", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-14", "event_date": "2026-08-13", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ukraine", "Russia", "OHCHR"]}
{"id": "2026-08-14-news-wildfires-spread-to-germany-and-croatia", "date": "2026-08-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Wildfires spread to Germany and Croatia", "summary": "Wildfires spread north and east across Europe, forcing fresh evacuations in Germany and Croatia three weeks into a persistent fire crisis.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/14/wildfires-force-thousands-to-flee-as-blazes-spread-across-europe", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing since 2026-07-23"], "topics": ["world", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Wildfires spread north and east across Europe, forcing fresh evacuations in Germany and Croatia three weeks into a persistent fire crisis. A blaze near the village of Gey in western Germany forced about 1,800 people from their homes, while strong winds drove a fire into the Croatian tourist town of Omiš and 525 residents fled a fire in the pine woods of France's Landes region. Al Jazeera reported roughly 500,000 hectares have burned across the EU so far this year. The flare-up extends an arc that began on 23 July with fires that killed three firefighters in France, Spain and Italy and later forced hundreds of thousands from homes near Bordeaux.", "why": "the fires are now reaching countries — Germany, Croatia — that were spared the late-July peak, underscoring how far the heat-and-drought season has spread across Switzerland's neighbours.", "thread_id": "2026-07-23-news-wildfires-kill-three-firefighters-across-france", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-23", "event_date": "2026-08-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Germany", "Croatia", "France", "European Union"]}
{"id": "2026-08-14-news-record-rain-kills-four-near-tokyo", "date": "2026-08-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Record rain kills four near Tokyo", "summary": "Unprecedented rainfall east of Tokyo killed four people and stranded thousands, with Japan issuing its top rain alert for Chiba for the first time.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/monde/des-pluies-sans-precedent-font-plusieurs-morts-pres-de-tokyo", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Record rainfall east of Tokyo killed four people and stranded thousands overnight into Friday 14 August. Torrential rain on Thursday evening prompted Japan's weather agency to issue its highest heavy-rain emergency warning for Chiba prefecture for the first time, triggering landslide alerts and power cuts; among the dead was a 66-year-old woman trapped in her car on a flooded road. Thousands were stranded at Narita International Airport and roughly 26,000 households lost power.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-08-14-news-record-rain-kills-four-near-tokyo", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-14", "event_date": "2026-08-13", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Japan", "Tokyo", "Chiba"]}
{"id": "2026-08-14-news-farage-wins-boycotted-clacton-by-election", "date": "2026-08-14", "stream": "news", "headline": "Farage wins boycotted Clacton by-election", "summary": "Reform UK leader Nigel Farage won the Clacton by-election he triggered by resigning, in a contest boycotted by the major parties.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/14/nigel-farage-defeats-count-binface-to-reclaim-uk-parliamentary-seat", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics", "world"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Reform UK leader Nigel Farage won back his Clacton seat in a by-election he himself triggered by resigning last month, in a contest boycotted by the major parties. Farage took 22,239 votes; his nearest challenger was the satirical candidate \"Count Binface\" with 9,455. Farage, who had faced allegations of financial impropriety, skipped the official count and cancelled a victory speech but called it a \"convincing, overwhelming win.\"", "why": "with mainstream parties standing aside, the low-competition result says less about national opinion than about Farage staging a confidence-boosting re-election for himself.", "thread_id": "2026-08-14-news-farage-wins-boycotted-clacton-by-election", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-14", "event_date": "2026-08-14", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Nigel Farage", "Reform UK", "Clacton"]}
